# .context — Siddharth Fit

## Project Purpose

Siddharth Fit is a premium personal-trainer portfolio and fitness-coaching website for a trainer named Siddharth. It serves as a lead-generation system where visitors learn about Siddharth, evaluate his expertise through achievements, certifications, and testimonials, review coaching plans with approximate pricing, and then contact him directly.

All payments, onboarding, and service delivery happen externally. The website does not process transactions.

## Brand Direction

Visual identity: Premium wellness studio, not hardcore bodybuilding advertisement.

Palette:

- Primary: Deep forest / muted emerald (health, growth, balance)
- Secondary: Sage (recovery, natural calm)
- Surface: Warm off-white / soft cream (human warmth)
- Accent: Muted teal (calmness, trust, modernity)
- Dark: Deep charcoal / near-black green (strength without aggression)
- Optional highlight: Soft amber (used sparingly)

Design language: Claymorphism + soft glass + controlled depth. Subtle, not inflated plastic. Large soft-radius cards, layered surfaces, low-contrast shadows, inset shadows, soft gradients.

Typography: Modern and highly readable. Inter / Geist / Manrope. Large display sizes for hero and section titles. Body at 16-18px.

The site should communicate: discipline, calm, trust, energy, professionalism, physical strength, mental clarity, consistency.

## Technical Constraints

- Next.js App Router with TypeScript (strict)
- SSR-first, Server Components by default
- Tailwind CSS for styling
- No database in v1
- No CMS in v1
- No authentication in v1
- No payment integration (ever on the website)
- Content driven by static TypeScript files in `/content/`
- `mailto:` for contact (no server-side email sending)
- Minimal dependencies

## Business Constraints

- No transactional language ("Buy Now", "Subscribe", "Checkout")
- Pricing is always "Starting from..." with CTA "Talk to Siddharth"
- No fabricated content (achievements, testimonials, credentials)
- No medical claims or fitness guarantees
- Real content must be supplied by Siddharth before production launch

## Content Rules

- All achievements, certificates, and testimonials must be real and verifiable
- Placeholder content must be clearly marked as `[PLACEHOLDER]`
- Testimonials require permission to publish name/photo
- Anonymous testimonials use "Verified Client"
- Social links only shown if Siddharth has an active account on that platform
- No decorative empty social icons

## Non-Goals (Version 1)

- Online payments
- User accounts / client dashboard
- Workout tracking
- Subscription billing
- Database
- CMS
- Appointment booking
- Automated email backend
- AI fitness recommendations
- Medical advice
- Social feed
- Blog (future route reserved)

## Future Direction

The architecture preserves a clean migration path:

```
Static content files
  --> JSON / MDX
    --> CMS API
      --> Database + Admin dashboard
        --> Micro-SaaS trainer platform
```

Possible future entities: Trainer, Client, Plan, Achievement, Certificate, Testimonial, Lead, Appointment, Workout, Exercise, ProgressRecord.

None of these should be prematurely implemented. The initial release stays static and lightweight.
